# KNOWN GAP -- CHAIN-LINK class, the VECTOR-RECEIVER cell of the `len` arm.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CELL THAT FALSIFIES A SCOPE CLAIM. `chain_link_bool_builtin.gg`
# carries `h.make().len()` as a live green row "pinning that the fix did not
# narrow the non-bool arms" -- but its receiver is a STRING. Swap the receiver
# for a `Vector[String]` and the SAME `len` arm is RED. A fixture's NAME is a
# claim about SCOPE (Core #12): that row pins the String-receiver cell only, and
# this file is the uncovered cell of the same axis.
#
# INTENDED OUTPUT: `2`. Rust gg answers `2` (regenerated 2026-08-29:
# `./target/debug/gg run tests/fixtures/known_gaps/chain_link_len_on_vector_method_result.gg`).
#
# TODAY the SELF-HOST emits C that will not compile:
#   error: incompatible types when assigning to type 'GorgetArray' from type 'size_t'
# Note the direction: here the CONTENDED key holds the receiver's `GorgetArray`
# and the value is the `size_t` length, the mirror of the String-receiver rows.
#
# PRE-EXISTING, not a regression: identical on a pristine `2d619258` driver.
#
# HEAP-FORCED: the receiver is a Vector field read back out of a struct.
#
# THE CLASS FIX is todo/t0712 (gate the name-list arms on the receiver type).
struct HV:
    Vector[String] v

equip HV:
    Vector[String] make(self):
        return self.v

void main():
    HV h = HV(["a", "b"])
    print(h.make().len())
